<p class="kicker">Lineage</p>
<h1>Standing on others' shoulders</h1>

<h2>Two quotations</h2>
<blockquote>
  <p>“He who receives an idea from me, receives instruction himself without lessening mine.”</p>
  <cite>Thomas Jefferson, letter to Isaac McPherson, August 13, 1813. Source: <a href="https://tjrs.monticello.org/letter/293">Monticello, Thomas Jefferson Retirement Series</a>.</cite>
</blockquote>
<p>Monticello's transcription keeps Jefferson's spelling: “he who recieves an idea from me, recieves instruction himself, without lessening mine;”. We use normalized spelling above. The letter is mostly about patents and inventions, so it shouldn't be read as Jefferson rejecting every form of copyright.</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>“Information should be free but your time should not.”</p>
  <cite>Steve Wozniak, replying to Stewart Brand at the 1984 Hackers Conference, as recounted by Steven Levy in <a href="https://www.wired.com/story/hackers-at-30-hackers-and-information-wants-to-be-free/">“Hackers at 30: ‘Hackers’ and ‘Information Wants to Be Free’”</a>, WIRED, November 21, 2014.</cite>
</blockquote>
<p>This comes from Levy's 2014 retrospective, not a 1984 transcript.</p>

